WEBVTT

00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:04.280
A collection plan translates the requirement into source priorities and lawful search

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.000
activities.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Break the main question into smaller information needs.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.045
For each need, identify likely source categories, expected evidence, collection order,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.000
time budget, and a clear owner.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.145
Prioritize sources by relevance, reliability, access, and cost.

00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:20.950
Official records or direct technical documentation may answer some questions efficiently.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.760
News, social sources, forums, imagery, maps,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.960
and archives may provide leads or context but often require more validation.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.000
Develop search concepts rather than one rigid query.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.200
Record key names, dates, products, locations,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.930
and public identifiers that are necessary to the requirement.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.980
Plan how terms may vary across languages or time.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.760
Search strategy should remain transparent and reproducible rather than relying on

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.930
unexplained intuition.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.210
Build legal and ethical constraints into the plan.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.950
Document approved public access, organizational policy, privacy boundaries,

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.000
handling requirements, and escalation points.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.095
Do not plan to bypass access controls, use deceptive identities,

00:00:56.095 --> 00:00:58.960
obtain stolen credentials, or enter spaces that are not legitimately available.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:00:59.930
Avoid overcollection.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.760
More data can increase false associations, privacy exposure, storage burden,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.925
and analytical noise.

00:01:04.925 --> 00:01:07.975
Collect the minimum material needed to evaluate the requirement.

00:01:07.975 --> 00:01:11.460
Sensitive personal information should not be gathered merely because it appears in a

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.200
result.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.000
Include contingencies.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.980
A source may disappear, conflict with another record, or prove unreliable.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:21.925
Identify alternatives and specify when to pause for legal, privacy, or supervisory review.

00:01:21.925 --> 00:01:26.095
A good collection plan focuses effort while leaving room to adapt when evidence changes

00:01:26.095 --> 00:01:26.850
the direction.
